Hello %FIRST, just a short explanation to the game:

(I think everyone knows how to play Tetris :-)

Scoring   : For every single piece you get a minimum of 1 Point, if
            you drop it, you'll get more according to the height.
            One cleared line makes 10 Points.
            Two in a row make 20 Points.
            Three in a row make 40 Points.
            Four in a row make 80 Points.

Speed     : Every cleared line increases the speed, the maximum is
            reached at 50 lines.

Highscores: there a 3 different highscore-tables:

    [A]lltimes : the best players of the BBS
    [M]onthly  : the best players of the last four weeks
    [W]eekly   : the players of the last 7 days

    additionally every player has his private highscore-table.


If you are the number one in any of the 3 highscore-tables, and
another player manages to push you back to number two, your
event.log will reflect this at your next login :-)

Your personal Preferences:

Using [C]onfig you can change the following settings:

how many Colors ?? --> the number of colors to be used (max. 8)
stretch display ?? --> hmm... my English is to bad in this case,
                       may your sysop find a solution :-)

inverse character  --> see ^^ (or simply try...)

which character ?? --> the character to be used to draw the pieces

(in most cases, an inverse space looks best, but with some
 graphic-adapters (hercules...) this is invisible :-)

At the end you can choose the keys that will be used for controlling
the pieces (default: 4,5,6 and space), be careful: we do NOT check
if you specify the same key for more than one function :-)

Best you can do is try it...

OK, you have now %TLCALL minutes left, before you get kicked off....
